 ship="<p>Florida&rsquo;s program is <a href=\"https://www.floridashine.org/\" rel=\"noopener\">SHINE &mdash; Serving Health Insurance Needs of Elders</a>, offered by the Florida Department of Elder Affairs and your local Area Agency on Aging, at <a href=\"tel:+18009635337\">1-800-963-5337</a> (TTY 1-800-955-8770). It is federally funded and free, and its counselors are trained volunteers who do not sell insurance; they help Medicare beneficiaries, families and caregivers compare plans, appeal denials and apply for Extra Help. In a state where 21.8% of residents are 65 or over &mdash; the fourth-highest share in the country in 2024 &mdash; SHINE is a good second opinion on anything an agent tells you. Program details as listed by <a href=\"https://www.shiphelp.org/ships/florida/\" rel=\"noopener\">shiphelp.org</a>.</p>",
